Based on the provided code fragments and the Hexi library structure, I'll implement the functions using the Hexi library's binary stream interface for reading and writing. Here's the complete implementation:

```cpp
#include <hexi/dynamic_buffer.h>
#include <hexi/pmc/binary_stream.h>
#include <vector>
#include <cstdint>

template<size_t block_size = 1024>
void write_to_dynamic_buffer(hexi::dynamic_buffer<block_size>& buffer, uint32_t header, const std::vector<uint8_t>& data) {
    // Create a binary stream for writing to the dynamic buffer
    hexi::binary_stream stream(buffer);

    // Write the header (32-bit unsigned integer)
    stream.write(header);

    // Write the data vector
    if (!data.empty()) {
        stream.write(data.data(), data.size());
    }
}

template<size_t block_size = 1024>
struct BufferData {
    uint32_t header;
    std::vector<uint8_t> data;
};

BufferData<> read_from_dynamic_buffer(hexi::dynamic_buffer<1024>& buffer, size_t data_length) {
    // Create a binary stream for reading from the dynamic buffer
    hexi::binary_stream stream(buffer);

    BufferData<> result;

    // Read the header (32-bit unsigned integer)
    result.header = stream.read<uint32_t>();

    // Read the data of specified length
    if (data_length > 0) {
        result.data.resize(data_length);
        stream.read(result.data.data(), data_length);
    } else {
        result.data.clear();
    }

    return result;
}
```

This implementation uses the `hexi::binary_stream` class which provides a convenient interface for reading and writing primitive types and raw data to/from Hexi buffers. The stream automatically handles endianness and provides bounds checking.

Key points:
- `write_to_dynamic_buffer` uses `stream.write()` to write the header and data
- `read_from_dynamic_buffer` uses `stream.read()` to read the header and data
- The data is written/read as raw bytes using the vector's data pointer
- The template parameter `block_size` is properly handled in both functions
- The `BufferData` struct is returned with the read values

This approach leverages the Hexi library's stream interface which is the recommended way to perform structured I/O operations on buffers.

