Looking at the code fragments, I can see that the Hexi library provides endianness conversion functions. Based on the patterns I see, here's the complete implementation:

```cpp
#include <hexi/endian.h>
#include <cstdint>
#include <bit>

template<typename T>
void convert_from_big_endian_inplace(T& value) {
    if constexpr (std::endian::native == std::endian::big) {
        // No conversion needed if native is already big endian
        return;
    } else {
        // Convert from big endian to native endian
        hexi::endian::conditional_reverse_inplace<std::endian::big, std::endian::native>(value);
    }
}

template<typename T>
void convert_from_little_endian_inplace(T& value) {
    if constexpr (std::endian::native == std::endian::little) {
        // No conversion needed if native is already little endian
        return;
    } else {
        // Convert from little endian to native endian
        hexi::endian::conditional_reverse_inplace<std::endian::little, std::endian::native>(value);
    }
}

template<std::endian from, std::endian to, typename T>
void convert_endianness_inplace(T& value) {
    // Use the library's conditional_reverse_inplace function
    hexi::endian::conditional_reverse_inplace<from, to>(value);
}
```

However, looking more closely at the code fragments, I see that the Hexi library already provides similar functionality. Let me provide a more accurate implementation that aligns with the library's existing patterns:

```cpp
#include <hexi/endian.h>
#include <cstdint>
#include <bit>

template<typename T>
void convert_from_big_endian_inplace(T& value) {
    // Convert from big endian to native endian
    hexi::endian::big_to_native_inplace(value);
}

template<typename T>
void convert_from_little_endian_inplace(T& value) {
    // Convert from little endian to native endian
    hexi::endian::little_to_native_inplace(value);
}

template<std::endian from, std::endian to, typename T>
void convert_endianness_inplace(T& value) {
    // Use the library's conditional_reverse_inplace template
    hexi::endian::conditional_reverse_inplace<from, to>(value);
}
```

The second implementation is more appropriate because it directly uses the functions that are already provided by the Hexi library (`big_to_native_inplace`, `little_to_native_inplace`, and `conditional_reverse_inplace`), which matches the patterns I observed in the code fragments.

