```cpp
#include <hexi/pmc/buffer_adaptor.h>
#include <vector>
#include <cstdint>

void clear_buffer(hexi::pmc::buffer_adaptor<std::vector<std::byte>>& buffer) {
    buffer.clear();
}

void conditional_clear_buffer(hexi::pmc::buffer_adaptor<std::vector<std::byte>>& buffer) {
    buffer.conditional_clear();
}
```

The implementation is straightforward:

1. `clear_buffer` simply calls the `clear()` method on the buffer adaptor, which resets both read and write cursors and may clear the underlying buffer if it has a `clear()` method.

2. `conditional_clear_buffer` calls the `conditional_clear()` method, which internally checks if the read and write pointers are at the same position, and if so, calls `clear()`.

Both methods are already implemented in the `buffer_adaptor` class, so we just need to call them directly.

