```cpp
#include <hexi/hexi.h>
#include <string>
#include <string_view>

void write_string_prefixed_varint(hexi::binary_stream& stream, const std::string& str) {
    stream << hexi::prefixed_varint(str);
}

std::string read_string_prefixed_varint(hexi::binary_stream& stream) {
    std::string str;
    stream >> hexi::prefixed_varint(str);
    return str;
}
```

The implementation follows the pattern shown in the test fragments:
- For writing: use `stream << hexi::prefixed_varint(str)`
- For reading: use `stream >> hexi::prefixed_varint(str)` where `str` is the target string variable

The `prefixed_varint` adaptor handles the variable-length integer encoding for the string length prefix automatically.

